{"title":"Bitwise Or Of All Subsequence Sums","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"Given an integer array nums, return the value of the bitwise OR of the sum of all possible subsequences in the array. A subsequence is a sequence that can be derived from another sequence by removing zero or more elements without changing the order of the remaining elements.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: nums = [2,1,0,3]\nOutput: 7\n```\n\nExplanation: All possible subsequence sums that we can have are: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6. And we have 0 OR 1 OR 2 OR 3 OR 4 OR 5 OR 6 = 7, so we return 7.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: nums = [0,0,0]\nOutput: 0\n```\n\nExplanation: 0 is the only possible subsequence sum we can have, so we return 0.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= nums.length <= 10^5\n- 0 <= nums[i] <= 10^9\n\nReturn the bitwise OR of the sums of all subsequences, including the empty subsequence. A bit is present in the result if some subsequence sum has that bit set. Individual elements expose their own set bits; lower bits can also carry into a bit when a subset of their residues crosses its halfway threshold.","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def subsequenceSumOr(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().subsequenceSumOr","parameters":[{"name":"nums","type":"List[int]"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":[[0,262]],"expected":262},{"input":[[0,992,147,1,95,347,771,345,463,867,203]],"expected":8191},{"input":[[0]],"expected":0},{"input":[[1,2,3]],"expected":7},{"input":[[1,830,663,788,241,670,670,488,760,742,908,352,699,822]],"expected":16383},{"input":[[10,984,764]],"expected":2046},{"input":[[101,157,256,180,407,262]],"expected":2047},{"input":[[101,425,792]],"expected":2047},{"input":[[104,557,631]],"expected":2047},{"input":[[104]],"expected":104},{"input":[[106,437,622]],"expected":2047},{"input":[[107,610,499,151,577]],"expected":2047},{"input":[[109,570,921,292,624,554,807,206,728,303,796,452,526,619]],"expected":8191},{"i